---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import LineChart from "../components/LineChart.astro";
import StackedBars from "../components/StackedBars.astro";
import fs from "node:fs";
import PeriodTable from "../components/PeriodTable.astro";
import { series, latest } from "../lib/data.js";
import { num, period } from "../lib/format.js";
const fx = latest(series("fx_reserves_total"));
const resChange = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync("src/data/generated/reserves_change.json", "utf8"));
---
<Base current="external" title="External">
  <h1>External sector</h1>
  <p class="lede">How large are India's foreign exchange reserves, and how is the rupee doing? Reserves were ${num(fx.value, 1)} billion in the week to {period(fx.period, "D")}.</p>

  <div class="grid2">
    <LineChart title="Foreign exchange reserves" subtitle="US$ billion, week ending Friday"
      lines={[{ id: "fx_reserves_total", label: "Total" }, { id: "fx_reserves_fca", label: "Foreign currency assets" }, { id: "fx_reserves_gold", label: "Gold" }]} years={1} />
    <LineChart title="USD/INR reference rate" subtitle="Rupees per US dollar, FBIL 1 pm fixing" lines={[{ id: "usdinr_ref" }]} years={1} />
  </div>
  <PeriodTable heading="US$ billion, week ended" n={6} rows={[
    { id: "fx_reserves_total", label: "Total reserves" }, { id: "fx_reserves_fca", indent: true }, { id: "fx_reserves_gold", indent: true },
  ]} freq="D" />
  <h3 id="rupee-reserves">The rupee and RBI's reserves</h3>
  <div class="grid2">
    <StackedBars title="Weekly change in reserves" subtitle="US$ billion, change on the previous week" rows={resChange.rows}
      interval="week" yLabel="US$ billion" legend={false} source="RBI Weekly Statistical Supplement; site calculation." />
    <LineChart title="USD/INR reference rate" subtitle="Rupees per US dollar (a higher rate is a weaker rupee)" lines={[{ id: "usdinr_ref" }]} years={1} />
  </div>
  <p class="chart-sub">RBI Weekly Statistical Supplement. Changes in reserves reflect RBI's market operations and valuation changes in currencies and gold, which the weekly data do not separate, so a fall is not the same as RBI selling dollars.</p>

  <h2 id="merchandise">Merchandise trade</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <LineChart title="Merchandise exports and imports" subtitle="US$ billion per month" lines={[{ id: "merch_imports", label: "Imports" }, { id: "merch_exports", label: "Exports" }]} years={3} />
    <LineChart title="Merchandise trade balance" subtitle="US$ billion per month" lines={[{ id: "merch_trade_balance", label: "Balance" }]} years={3} />
  </div>
  <PeriodTable heading="US$ billion" n={6} digits={1} rows={[
    { id: "merch_exports" }, { id: "merch_exports", how: "yoy", label: "  % y/y", indent: true },
    { id: "merch_imports" }, { id: "merch_imports", how: "yoy", label: "  % y/y", indent: true },
    { id: "merch_trade_balance" },
  ]} />
  <p class="chart-sub">Department of Commerce (monthly SDDS table). The latest month is provisional; the following year's release revises it, and the revised value is used.</p>

  <h2 id="services">Services trade</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <LineChart title="Services exports and imports" subtitle="US$ billion per month" lines={[{ id: "services_exports", label: "Exports" }, { id: "services_imports", label: "Imports" }]} years={2} />
    <LineChart title="Services trade growth, as published" subtitle="% change on the same month a year earlier" lines={[{ id: "services_exports_growth", label: "Exports" }, { id: "services_imports_growth", label: "Imports" }]} years={2} />
  </div>
  <p class="chart-sub">RBI's monthly data on trade in services, about 45 days after the month; the latest two months are provisional. India runs a large surplus on services, which offsets much of the merchandise deficit. Shown with attribution; download pending a check of RBI's terms.</p>

  <h2 id="bop">Balance of payments</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <LineChart title="Current account balance" subtitle="% of GDP, quarterly (negative = deficit)" lines={[{ id: "bop_cab_pct_gdp", label: "Current account" }]} years={4} />
    <LineChart title="Capital flows" subtitle="US$ billion per quarter, net" lines={[{ id: "bop_fdi_net", label: "Foreign direct investment" }, { id: "bop_portfolio_net", label: "Portfolio investment" }]} years={4} />
  </div>
  <PeriodTable heading="US$ billion, net" n={5} digits={1} freq="Q" rows={[
    { id: "bop_current_account", label: "Current account" }, { id: "bop_goods_net", label: "Goods", indent: true },
    { id: "bop_services_net", label: "Services", indent: true }, { id: "bop_primary_income_net", label: "Primary income", indent: true },
    { id: "bop_secondary_income_net", label: "Secondary income (mainly remittances)", indent: true },
    { id: "bop_cab_pct_gdp", label: "Current account, % of GDP" },
    { id: "bop_fdi_net", label: "Net FDI" }, { id: "bop_portfolio_net", label: "Net portfolio flows" },
  ]} />
  <LineChart title="Current account, monthly" subtitle="US$ billion (RBI's monthly balance of payments, published since 2026; preliminary)" lines={[{ id: "bop_cab_monthly", label: "Current account" }]} years={2} />
  <p class="chart-sub">RBI's balance-of-payments releases. The latest quarter is preliminary and each release revises the same quarter a year earlier; we keep the latest figure.</p>

  <h2 id="remittances">Remittances</h2>
  <LineChart title="Remittances" subtitle="US$ billion a quarter: personal transfer receipts, gross"
    lines={[{ id: "bop_remittances", label: "Personal transfer receipts" }]} years={4} />
  <p class="chart-sub">RBI describes personal transfer receipts as mainly remittances by Indians employed overseas. Taken from the text of each quarterly balance-of-payments release, which has printed this figure since Q3 2024-25 (with the year-earlier quarter), so the series starts in Q3 2023-24.</p>

  <h2 id="eer">Effective exchange rates</h2>
  <LineChart title="The rupee against a basket of 64 economies" subtitle="Index, 2020 = 100, monthly average; a rise means a stronger rupee"
    lines={[{ id: "reer_bis_broad", label: "Real (REER)" }, { id: "neer_bis_broad", label: "Nominal (NEER)" }]} reference={{ target: 100 }} years={10} />
  <p class="chart-sub">The nominal index weights the rupee's exchange rates by trade; the real index also adjusts for inflation in India relative to its trading partners. Source: Bank for International Settlements, broad indices. RBI publishes its own 40-currency indices in its monthly Bulletin, but those tables have no stable links for us to read; the BIS indices use a different base and weights, so their levels differ from RBI's.</p>

  <h2 id="debt">External debt</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <LineChart title="External debt" subtitle="US$ billion, end of quarter"
      lines={[{ id: "external_debt", label: "External debt" }]} years={4} />
    <LineChart title="External debt to GDP" subtitle="%, end of quarter"
      lines={[{ id: "external_debt_pct_gdp", label: "Debt / GDP" }]} years={4} />
  </div>
  <p class="chart-sub">From the highlights of RBI's quarterly external debt releases (each gives the latest quarter and the one it is compared with). RBI's press-release index currently lists only the end-March and end-June releases, so other quarters are missing. Changes include valuation effects from exchange-rate moves.</p>

  <h2>Still to come on this page</h2>
  <p class="chart-sub">External commercial borrowing (ECB). Checklist: docs/guidebook/05-pages/external.md.</p>
</Base>
